                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It is difficult to give a negative review to a work of someone whom I greatly admire, especially when he gives it for free - but I think honesty is more important. \nGeneral idea for this demo is absolutely great - a very personal, story-driven VR half-interactive psychedelic illustration book. It seems like a very powerful tool to convey ideas and tell stories, but in order to work it needs one thing - it needs to be done with great attention to details. As it is, \"Delia's gift\" is more of a very rough sketch than a complete experience. The art seems more like a placeholder, sound quality is very poor, and many of the story's pages do not have any weight to them.\nI am not writing this to discourage you Cabbio, as I said - I absolutely admire your work, but as I said, I believe it needs much more polish to really work in I way I imagine you designed it for. The story could have much more impact if accompanied by a more fleshed out scenery. I mean, if the story is really that personal to you - take more time it and give it more LOVE:)\n23+93!",
